<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">South Brunswick, New Jersey</p>
    <h1>Stop the data center at 4405 Route 1</h1>
    <p class="lede">A data center going up near homes on Route 1 wants a state permit for 12 diesel generators, with no limit on emergency use and no monitoring of what comes out.</p>
    <p class="deadline" data-until="2026-11-09"><strong>Comments to NJDEP are due November 9.</strong> <a href="/comment/">Here's how →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap section">
  <h2>Three things to know</h2>
  <div class="three">
    <div class="point">
      <h3>Power</h3>
      <p>Likely uses more electricity than every home in South Brunswick combined, around the clock. Its backup generators alone total about 43 megawatts.</p>
      <a class="cite" href="/south-brunswick/#power">Details and sources</a>
    </div>
    <div class="point">
      <h3>Noise</h3>
      <p>Cooling equipment that runs 24/7, plus 12 diesel engines tested during the day. No one has shown whether the noise study measured low-frequency hum.</p>
      <a class="cite" href="/south-brunswick/#noise">Details and sources</a>
    </div>
    <div class="point">
      <h3>Air</h3>
      <p>When all 12 generators run, the permit allows as much smog-forming NOx per hour as a 600-megawatt coal plant. NOx worsens asthma, and diesel exhaust causes cancer.</p>
      <a class="cite" href="/south-brunswick/#air">Details and sources</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

